Stage 3: OK/CANCEL dialog CLOSE path -- fix the CANCEL return-to-menu SIGSEGV in the shared
cb74/cb7c list-dialog front-end (all asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin).

ROOT CAUSE (FIST_SEGV_BT + pattern-init deterministic repro; fault-addr 0x3776, EIP in cb74).
FUN_0000_cb74 and FUN_0000_cb7c share one code body from cb82 (two entry points differing only by the
DAT_2000_a82e flag).  Its tail, after the modal loop cc33 returns, copies the selected 8.3 name to the
caller's dest.  The asm:

    cb9e: call 0xcc33            ; modal list dialog
    cba1: jb   0xcbcb            ; CF (CANCEL, a85d>=2) -> SKIP the copy, return a85d
    cba3: mov  di,[0xe855]       ; dest = ds:di (caller's DGROUP dest ptr == param_7)
    cba7: mov  es,[0x70]         ; src seg = STRSEG (word[DGROUP:0x70])
    cbab: mov  si,[0xe838]       ; si = a838 (selected row)
    cbaf: shl  si,4
    cbb2: add  si,0x3776         ; src = STRSEG:(a838*0x10 + 0x3776)
    cbb6..cbbe: rep movsb 13     ; copy 13 bytes es:si -> ds:di
    cbc0: pop  [0x452]; clc; ret
    cbc6: (a834==0) mov [0xe85d],4
    cbcb: pop  [0x452]; mov al,[0xe85d]; stc; ret

Ghidra (a) DROPPED the `jb cbcb` branch (bVar7 hardcoded false) so the copy ran unconditionally, and
(b) BASE-LOST the source: `es:si` became the raw host pointer `a838*0x10 + 0x3776` == 0x3776 for the
first row -> deref of linear 0x3776 -> SIGSEGV on the return-to-menu after CANCEL.  It also invented
`DAT_1000_c452 = unaff_CS` for the `push/pop [0x452]` save/restore -> clobbered the click-timestamp
c452 with an uninitialised value (the flaky-garbage class of patches 125-128; deterministic only under
-ftrivial-auto-var-init=pattern, which is why plain gdb masked it).

FIX (faithful): thread cc33's carry (the shim global g_fist_cf, set by cc33's patch-142 exit to
a85d>=2 == CANCEL); on CANCEL skip the copy and return a85d.  On OK/select copy 13 bytes from the
correctly-based source STRSEG:(a838*0x10+0x3776) to param_7 (the caller's DGROUP dest pointer, held in
di unchanged across the call).  Preserve c452 across the call (save/restore, matching push/pop [0x452]).
Applied to BOTH cb74 and cb7c (shared body).  cbd4 carries the same idiom but is on the mission-load
path (not the menu dispatch) and is not reached by any covered flow -- left as documented latent debt.

NOTE the return value / CF is IGNORED by the e714 dispatch cases (they set b78e=10 = menu-idle and
continue regardless), so CANCEL cleanly restores the plain menu; a genuine DOSBox CANCEL capture
(ref/cancel_native320.png, CAMPAIGNS dialog -> CANCEL @205,140) is AE=0 on both targets.

